WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.257
Now it is your turn to apply the workflow independently.

00:00:03.257 --> 00:00:09.372
Start by creating a DataFrame with at least eight rows or loading a small CSV file.

00:00:09.372 --> 00:00:16.107
Then inspect it. Show the first rows, the shape, the data types, missing values, and duplicates.

00:00:16.107 --> 00:00:20.312
Next, identify at least one issue that needs cleaning.

00:00:20.312 --> 00:00:24.707
It could be a data type, a text category, a missing value, or a duplicate.

00:00:24.707 --> 00:00:30.412
After cleaning, create at least one useful derived column.

00:00:30.412 --> 00:00:34.142
Then use groupby or pivot_table to answer a question about the data.

00:00:34.142 --> 00:00:35.562
Do not stop when the code runs.

00:00:35.562 --> 00:00:41.237
Write two sentences explaining what your result means.

00:00:41.237 --> 00:00:48.282
Then write one limitation. For example, you might say that one category has the highest average value,

00:00:48.282 --> 00:00:50.027
but the dataset is small or covers only one month.

00:00:50.027 --> 00:00:55.887
There is no single required solution for this exercise.

00:00:55.887 --> 00:01:01.863
The goal is to demonstrate that you can make reasonable analytical decisions and explain why you made them.
